>> title: Panna Cotta
>> category: Custards & Puddings
>> tags: cream, gelatin, vanilla, no-bake, make-ahead
>> counters: Pizzeria
>> servings: 6
>> time: 4 hr 30 min
>> slack: narrow — the cream is hot and never boiling, because boiling weakens the gelatin and a panna cotta that will not stand cannot be re-set

>> step: bloom 5 min
Sprinkle @unflavored gelatin{2%tsp}(7 g, one envelope) over @cold water{3%Tbs}(45 mL) and let it bloom for ~{5%min}.

Heat @heavy cream{2%cup}(480 mL), @whole milk{1%cup}(240 mL), @table salt{1/8%tsp} in a #saucepan{} until it steams.

>> step: stir in the sugar
Stir @granulated sugar{1/3%cup}(65 g), @vanilla bean{1%whole}(split, seeds scraped in) into @&(~1)hot cream{}.

>> step: whisk in the gelatin
Whisk @&(~3)bloomed gelatin{} into @&(~1)sweetened cream{}.

Pour @&(~1)base{} into #6 ramekins{} and chill for ~{4%hr}.
